{{also|over|över|Över|øver|över-}}
==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{m|enm|over-}}, from {{etyl|ang|en}} {{m|ang|ofer-||over-}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|en}} {{m|gem-pro|*ubar-||over-}}. Cognate with {{cog|nl|over-}}, {{cog|de|über-}}, {{cog|da|over-}}, {{cog|sv|över-}}. More at {{l|en|over}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|en|/ˈəʊvə/}}
* {{a|GA}} {{IPA|en|/ˈoʊvɚ/}}

===Prefix===
{{en-prefix}}

# [[above]], or [[higher]]
# [[superior]]
# [[excessive]]ly
#: {{m|en|overkind}}, {{m|en|overloud}}
# [[surrounding]] or [[covering]]
#: {{m|en|overcoat}}, {{m|en|overpack}}, {{m|en|overshoe}}

====Usage notes====
Comparison of relative combinations (two separate words, hyphenated or a single compound word) does not easily fit a pattern; terms become compound words as they are broadly accepted.

